<title>FINLAND: Finnish T-bill auction raises 1.00 bln markka.</title>
<headline>Finnish T-bill auction raises 1.00 bln markka.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of the State Treasury Office's T-Bills auction on Tuesday compared to the October 1 auction  SUVK :</p>
<p>				This auction	Previous auction</p>
<p>				187-day T-bills   194-day T-bills</p>
<p> Av. yield, pct	   3.15 pct	    3.28 pct</p>
<p> Highest accepted	 3.15 pct	    3.28 pct</p>
<p> Lowest accepted	  3.14 pct	    3.28 pct</p>
<p> Amount, FIM million	  480		   400</p>
<p> Bids, million mk	     2,690		 1,643</p>
<p> Maturing date	    April 15, 1997    April 15, 1997</p>
<p>				This auction	Previous auction</p>
<p>				340-day T-bills   347-day T-bills</p>
<p> Av. yield, pct	   3.29 pct	    3.48 pct</p>
<p> Highest accepted	 3.29 pct	    3.48 pct</p>
<p> Lowest accepted	  3.29 pct	    3.47 pct</p>
<p> Amount, million mk	   520		   760</p>
<p> Bids, million mk	     1,540		 1,176</p>
<p> Maturing date	    Sept 15, 1997     Sept 15, 1997</p>
<p>Total planned issue amount was 1.0 billion markka. After today's auction, the outstanding amount of treasury bills is 50,324 million markka, the STO said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358 - 0 - 680 50 245</p>
</text>
